+# Local synthetic SDK callback source contract
+
+Scope: owner06 mock input contract only. Existing API `offmenu-mocks/1` and strict Identity semantics `offmenu-identity-session/2` remain unchanged. This result adds no redirect, HTTP route, browser session, consent flow or state store. Native `/authorize` and `/callback` still return501.
+
+Agreed with Worker04: its LOCAL harness creates a callback fragment only after explicit same-tab intent. The retained guard accepts access_token, refresh_token, token_type, expires_in, expires_at and provider; duplicates, mixed token kinds and unsupported state/nonce/redirect fields fail before SDK handling. Provider/start time is kept in same-tab sessionStorage, limited to15minutes, consumed once; absent/stale/future/wrong-provider/replayed intent fails and the URL is scrubbed. This is an accidental-response guard, not cryptographic OAuth state/nonce verification. Netlify server OAuth state verification remains a separate provider boundary. Consent and linking are unknown.
+
+## Source interface
+
+`callbackSourceTokenRequest(actorId)` returns the exact known synthetic password-grant request for Alice, Bob or admin. The caller sends it through the selected local `createOutboundAdapter`; the function itself does no I/O. The named HTTPS URL identifies the existing mock contract and is not an instruction to call a live provider.
+
+After a newly observed native HTTP200 token response, `validateCallbackSourceReply(actorId,reply,{httpStatus,localOrigin})` checks an explicit literal-loopback HTTP origin/port and all four native fixture fields. It rejects wrong actors, mixed access/refresh pairs, changed expiry/type, missing fields, callback/provider fields or invented consent. The returned token fields are frozen. Matching fixed synthetic token bytes does not establish that the actor is currently unrevoked, signed in, provider-authenticated or consented. Caller must use native user/refresh checks and the Worker04 guard. `currentSessionVerified` and `providerAcceptance` are explicitly false.
+
+Worker04 owns fragment construction, intent consumption, SDK invocation, URL scrubbing and callback UI. Owner06 owns native synthetic token/user/refresh/logout behavior. Worker02 owns central app/browser composition. Worker05 owns preview/runtime lifecycle. No peer source or existing19076process is modified here.
+
+## Remaining original-scope gates
+
+- Real Google authorization/callback and provider consent/linking remain unsupported501; this contract never qualifies them.
+- Browser extension/native bridge interface is not agreed. Device/health bridges are not HTTP mocks. No fabricated native success fixture is added.
+- Other provider/service scenarios need exact method/path/header/request and response assertions from the app/provider owner before a new fixture is implemented.
+- Independent12/58 qualification and a fresh Worker05-owned runtime/source pin are required before adoption. This source result is not self-accepted.
+
+## Evidence
+
+New callback-source contract has five focused tests; unchanged base mock validation retains128 tests. Combined run:133passed,0failed. The16original mock files were restored and independently byte-checked against9b31f7d. No fresh Java runtime was started for this pure validator change and no new live06lease exists. Existing9b31 real-Java/Identity/logout receipts remain preserved;05owns19076. Worker04 separately reports4installed-SDK/native9b31tests passed, nativeaudit23requests0unmatched and owned shutdown in its836f7dd candidate; that evidence is owner-reported, not independent acceptance of this new module.
+
+Catalogue auxiliary source8f23c3d is frozen outside checkout at `/home/user/src/offmenu-data/worker-06-private-catalogue-20261014/source-8f23c3d`,23951source bytes; its data/index remain referenced, not copied. Historical855715PID was absent and19166closed on pickup. One restored private viewer is owned by06(PID959569,birth2455715,run96fa35b48d7a4abebd0a96fc8392f31d), and serves25135main records before/after the original mock branch switch. Production publication remains cancelled; no Netlify continuation.
